# Rabin capture, workflow routing and drawing geometry checkpoint

REA Studio remains a development collection of ten applications. **Zero products have established full replacement status.** The accepted objective remains every documented feature and comparative speed, resource use, usability, compatibility and reliability. The [acceptance conditions](ACCEPTANCE.md) and [status](STATUS.json) keep those requirements open. This checkpoint implements bounded capabilities and records finite evidence; it is not a completion certificate.

## Implemented behavior

Backup now uses a source-assisted degree-53 Rabin rolling fingerprint for supported native restic file captures: a 64-byte window, three authenticated polynomials, a 512 KiB minimum and an 8 MiB maximum chunk. A bounded streaming capture checks cancellation/deadline/owned lock state around file operations, preserves primary errors during cleanup, and retains post-commit cleanup failures as warnings. Native v1/v2 encryption, compression, inspection, integrity checks and restore remain available.

Automation adds bounded released-version Switch 3.4 routing and Merge 3.2 append, choose-branch, position, Cartesian and field joins. The editor exposes input/output ports and rejects ambiguous input connections. Acyclic manual workflows preserve input buffers across interval Wait/restart, clear terminal buffers and retain histories. The independent review found two additional defects in the first integration: checkpoint delay could consume the remaining active deadline before HTTP, and a contradictory saved downstream invocation could issue an extra request. The exact failure evidence is preserved. Current recovery compares queued/buffered items with immediate completed predecessor outputs, rechecks the active deadline after awaited checkpoint writes, and checks cancellation/deadline/per-item timeout before HTTP inputs and redirects. Structural consistency is not checkpoint authentication or a complete graph-prefix proof; cooperative checks cannot preempt blocked I/O or guarantee remote delivery.

Sketch adds signed straight native lines and unrotated diamonds to the editable scene, geometric selection, grouped movement, history and safe SVG/native export. Negative line dimensions retain endpoint direction. Diamond polygon anchors follow the released helper's floor/plus-one behavior within an explicit tiny-dimension clamp deviation. Unsupported/rotated native records remain opaque. A separate collector follow-up bounds test child execution/output and preserves historical receipt identity. Its17 synthetic process groups pass in root integration and independent review; child roots/grandchildren recorded by that finite corpus are absent afterward. Exited-root orphan cleanup and bootstrap/fingerprint/publication I/O deadlines remain gaps.

## Methods and authority

The Backup comparison authenticates the complete restic 0.19.1 Windows executable before every original execution. Its [47-check integration receipt](apps/backup/results/rabin-validation.json) records 30 original file cases matching 126 ordered chunk boundaries/IDs, plus four candidate snapshot original check/restore executions. The lifecycle collection contains 20 production observations and three strict expired-I/O cases. Source-assisted chunking is attributed to the preserved BSD-2-Clause restic/chunker source. These tests do not establish arbitrary settings, special files, full metadata or storage-backend behavior.

The [first Automation routing receipt](apps/automation/results/routing-validation.json) records 56 native/original tests plus three editor regressions. Its authenticated n8n 2.16.0 selected source execution comprises 114 Switch node executions and 1,759 Merge mode-helper executions:1,812 exact outputs,10 error-presence outcomes, three deliberate unsafe-key deviations and 48 array-representation deviations. Seven enqueue helper executions and four extracted drain-block executions remain separate. The full released scheduler, Merge class, defaults, SQL modes, server and editor were not run by that collection. The [routing contract](apps/automation/ROUTING.md) documents the finite runtime bounds and unsupported behavior. The [current recovery receipt](apps/automation/results/recovery-followup/integration-validation.json) passes74 groups, including ten added recovery and five HTTP boundary groups, with 43 current source identities stable. Its raw original count is unchanged. The [independent review preservation](apps/automation/results/recovery-followup/independent-review/preservation-manifest.json) retains57 exact artifacts and the corrected source/guards review.

The [Sketch geometry receipt](apps/sketch/results/geometry-validation.json) records 28 passing tests,17 comparative contexts and 35 direct original helper/restoration/serializer calls. Six legacy individual restorations are a separate corpus count; they do not total every call performed by that older harness. The @excalidraw/excalidraw0.18.1 archive, bundle and source map are authenticated, and 25 extracted helper ranges are byte-identical to their mapped released sources. The [independent review](apps/sketch/results/geometry-independent-review/preservation-manifest.json) additionally checks528 geometric hit points and preserves a separate source-reference accounting correction. Original rough rendering, binding repair and hosted-service behavior remain unverified.

Test results bind exact source bytes, original identities, raw output, collector versions and before/after inventories. Inert source snapshots preserve unsuccessful attempts and earlier implementations. Passing a current run does not rebind an old receipt to changed code. The Backup recorder follow-up corrects Node24.16 TAP comment escaping, exercises a fresh90 KB live child logger and preserves the initial inherited-context failure; it does not rerun or relabel the earlier47 Backup behavior checks.

## Interactive checks

The [frozen browser checkpoint](results/milestones/rabin-routing-geometry-browser-20261012/snapshot-manifest.json) preserves82 implementation sources, three focused receipts and 14 browser artifacts. It predates the Automation recovery and Sketch collector follow-ups. Five Backup interface operations created, captured, inspected, checked and restored an encrypted synthetic repository; the original executable also checked and restored it, with four files totaling18,874,552 bytes matching exactly. Password fields were cleared.

The first Automation browser run rejected a conflicting connection, saved a valid six-step Switch/Wait/Merge graph, completed it, and reopened its saved history after reload. This predates the subsequently discovered recovery defects. A [fresh parent-owned current-source Automation check](results/browser-automation-recovery-20261012/validation.json) passed five checks on a separate newly started host: graph validation, revision 1 save, a six-step completed run, and the same exact saved run after browser reload, with 41 source identities unchanged. Reload is not a host restart; adversarial recovery and HTTP boundary proof comes from the74-check backend collection. Sketch drew a signed line and a diamond in reverse direction, grouped and moved them by the same35/25 offset, verified exact undo/redo, saved/reloaded the scene, and downloaded Studio JSON, native .excalidraw and SVG through real controls. Those exports retain signed endpoint vectors and grouping. The 82-source before/after interval covers the subsequent Sketch work; timestamps are not backdated to earlier Backup/Automation actions.

## Unaccepted Metrics experiments

The [preserved measurement study](results/metrics-dispatch-observations-20261012/README.md) includes separate standard-dispatch and percentile candidates,210 timing children,210 isolated-memory children,852,516 memory output/cache checks,840 raw memory logs and six source-bound figures. All measurement children passed with no measured limit hits. **Neither candidate is accepted; the production reducer remains unchanged.**

The standard candidate's p95 median regressed1.42% against baseline. The percentile candidate improved the fixed single-p95 median but regressed all99/all124 medians10.22%/4.45% against baseline. Several control ranges overlap; causality and statistical significance are unestablished. The large original bulk-percentile difference already belongs to baseline. Baseline and percentile candidate have identical 68,792-byte median retained-minus-released p95 heap differences, so smaller result-object footprint is not established. Negative deltas are preserved, not clipped. Root coordinated a quiet interval 20:26:14–20:38:55 UTC, while unrelated Windows background work remained uncontrolled. Memory sequences exceeded provisional duration estimates. Archive originals remain local; public preservation contains exact selected sources/logs/figures and applicable licenses.

## Validation and remaining work

The first combined run executed607 tests and passed605. Both failures stopped native v1/v2 interoperability tests at the inherited `saved.newPacks >= 7` assumption; Rabin chunking changes the number of data blobs even before pack aggregation. The [failure record](results/full-suite-recovery-followup/failed-607/failure-validation.json) preserves raw output and exact selected post-failure sources. It does not claim whole-run source stability. The replacement assertion authenticates physical pack hashes, encrypted headers/payloads, index rows and all snapshot content IDs, then verifies unchanged data-pack/index identities on a repeat backup. Existing original check/restore assertions remain. The [focused follow-up](apps/backup/results/native-policy-followup/validation.json) records its actual outcome separately. Pack aggregation remains stage-only.

The [KeePass manual supplement](requirements/keepass-manual-supplement/README.md) records 199 selected contracts across10 topics and a separate census of all45 HTML topics/139 extracted files.15 documentation-integrity checks pass; zero original or candidate behavior executions are claimed. Exact carrier/topic/span/context hashes retain citation identity, while full manual sources and carriers stay local.35 HTML topics and broader platform/protocol/security/plugin/import/export matrices remain open. This supplement preserves the existing159 source/API fingerprints and 232 capability IDs separately.

The [current combined validation](results/development-validation.json) records **607/607 passing tests**, zero skips/failures/cancellations/todo, and 611 exact source fingerprints unchanged throughout the run. Private generated data/original caches and inert historical test snapshots are excluded from runnable test discovery. The [current Sketch collector receipt](apps/sketch/results/collector-followup/integration-validation.json) records 17 groups and five unchanged collector/test sources, with 54 stage,27 adapter and 21 independent-review artifacts preserved separately. The [Backup recorder receipt](apps/backup/results/rabin-recorder-review/integration-validation.json) records eight tests. The public commit identity is verified after publication in the ignored local publication receipt; no pre-publication commit is invented. The historical [496-test compression/remote checkpoint](COMPRESSION-REMOTE-MILESTONE.md) is preserved at public revision b9f6b71b215028d786af5eaa3d41ae46cc3ec9ac with seven receipts and 369 sources. Earlier development checkpoints remain intact.

Every whole-product feature gate remains open. The 232 capability-area rows and 159 original source/API fingerprints are initial discovery records, not exhaustive feature extraction. Complete product/platform/edition binding, every documented option, compatible originals' fixtures, unsupported runtime/editor/tool behaviors, long-run fault reliability, comparative usability, production security and whole-product performance all remain required. Bounded finite progress is retained without reducing the user's completion scope.
